# --- PRIVATE SIGNING KEYS NEVER ENTER THIS REPO ---
# Policy: src/s0/data/keys/README.md. The issuing authority's private key is generated
# out-of-band and stays out-of-band. Only public keys are committed.
**/*private*.pem
!src/s0/data/keys/demo_issuer_private.pem
**/*private*.key
**/*private*.der
src/s0/data/keys/demo_issuer.key

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
public/
# `site/` was ignored here as the Sphinx/mkdocs HTML output convention. Nothing
# in this repo builds to it -- the docs are GitBook, hosted, validated by
# tools/build-docs.sh with no local build -- and it is now the Cloudflare Pages
# deploy root (landing page, installer, verifier), so it must stay tracked.
.venv/

# Wipe test artifacts (disk images can be large)
*.img
*.raw
tests/cli/tmp/
demo-out/
sanitization_reports/

# OS
.DS_Store
tmp/
/tmp/
*.db

# Agent tools
.agents/
skills-lock.json

.env*

# Local test artifacts produced by portal PDF verification runs
site/verify/tests/x*.pdf

# Stray package downloads
*.whl

# Working plan: kept local and untracked by request
docs/project/industry-plan.md

# Keypairs generated by `s0 keygen` in the working tree
operator_key_*.pem
custom_issuer_*.pem

# Compliance artifacts written by a run in the repository root.
#
# `s0 wipe` defaults to `default_out_dir: demo-out`, but a run from the repo root
# with an explicit --out-dir, or the file-erase path, writes certificates, PDFs and
# QR codes straight into the working directory. 69 of these were committed by
# accident. They are outputs, not sources: never track them.
file_wipe_certificate_*
wipe_certificate_*
carve_manifest_*
acquisition_manifest_*
*.qr.png
demo-out/
.wrangler/
